(493435, 48281, 9387, '<td valign="top">I love the idea and the portrayal.  One question though -- if it is a woman leaving her husband for his father --why the man''s wedding ring?  From the ring I get the idea that it is one guy leaving another guy for the father.  This in no way affected the outcome of the score I gave you.  Just a personal thought.  The picture and the idea behind it (which ever scenario one chooses to think) is great.  Good luck!</td>', 'I love the idea and the portrayal.  One question though -- if it is a woman leaving her husband for his father --why the man''s wedding ring?  From the ring I get the idea that it is one guy leaving another guy for the father.  This in no way affected the outcome of the score I gave you.  Just a personal thought.  The picture and the idea behind it (which ever scenario one chooses to think) is great.  Good luck!', '2003-11-24 10:22:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(493437, 47791, 9387, '<td valign="top">Great thought and good picture.  My only thought is that I don''t like the circle of light by the pin.  If you would have tried to do this in natural light on your tripod I think it would have looked better.  All in all though a very good depiction of the challenge and I''m sure it was hard to get that pin in the balloon before it actually did break.  LOL --another good photo --a picture of the person holding the pin when the balloon did break.</td>', 'Great thought and good picture.  My only thought is that I don''t like the circle of light by the pin.  If you would have tried to do this in natural light on your tripod I think it would have looked better.  All in all though a very good depiction of the challenge and I''m sure it was hard to get that pin in the balloon before it actually did break.  LOL --another good photo --a picture of the person holding the pin when the balloon did break.', '2003-11-24 10:24:35.000000', NULL, 1),
