(499595, 48324, 806, '<td valign="top">beautiful photograph.. congrats!<br/>love the feeling of surprise, and the entire emotion of this image! great choice of b&amp;w!</td>', 'beautiful photograph.. congrats!love the feeling of surprise, and the entire emotion of this image! great choice of b&w!', '2003-12-01 00:31:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(499623, 48141, 12253, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the critique club:<br/> <br/>This has a nice science fiction feel to it, and if I am correct you are assuming we''ve seen enough science fiction to guess that what''s in his hands might be surprising.  For me that works, though I am not sure it would for everyone.  <br/> <br/>Compositionally, I think its framed well for this shot.  The lighting is especially interesting and appropriate here.  However, perhaps to get the effect the saturation on the red was set a bit too high, and that gives it a softer focus, and in some places, almost a posterized look that I am a little mixed about (good for effect, but makes the image look lower quality).<br/> <br/>I am not sure the model and photo is "gallery ready" but you''ve used good imagination here and captured it well.<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the critique club: This has a nice science fiction feel to it, and if I am correct you are assuming we''ve seen enough science fiction to guess that what''s in his hands might be surprising.  For me that works, though I am not sure it would for everyone.   Compositionally, I think its framed well for this shot.  The lighting is especially interesting and appropriate here.  However, perhaps to get the effect the saturation on the red was set a bit too high, and that gives it a softer focus, and in some places, almost a posterized look that I am a little mixed about (good for effect, but makes the image look lower quality). I am not sure the model and photo is "gallery ready" but you''ve used good imagination here and captured it well.', '2003-12-01 00:57:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(499629, 47747, 12253, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the critique club:<br/> <br/>I think this shot is very good compositionally, and most of the technical elements within your control are well done.  The neck has some overexposed areas, but this works for me as part of the aesthetics of the shot.<br/> <br/>Aesthetically, overall, I rate this photo very good.<br/> <br/>I suspect this is a small portion of a larger frame, and this implicitly lower resolution, and perhaps your overall camera resolution, are lowering the subjective quality of the capture.  (Consider the deer''s fur on it''s side and hind and you''ll see some of the quality issue I am talking about.)<br/> <br/>I understand how this might be a surprise to both of you, but personally I think this image would have been hurt topically in the surprise challenge because many won''t see this as surprise.<br/> <br/>Overall, this is a beautiful photo.<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the critique club: I think this shot is very good compositionally, and most of the technical elements within your control are well done.  The neck has some overexposed areas, but this works for me as part of the aesthetics of the shot. Aesthetically, overall, I rate this photo very good. I suspect this is a small portion of a larger frame, and this implicitly lower resolution, and perhaps your overall camera resolution, are lowering the subjective quality of the capture.  (Consider the deer''s fur on it''s side and hind and you''ll see some of the quality issue I am talking about.) I understand how this might be a surprise to both of you, but personally I think this image would have been hurt topically in the surprise challenge because many won''t see this as surprise. Overall, this is a beautiful photo.', '2003-12-01 01:06:18.000000', NULL, 0),
